          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "雪人 (xuěrén) is built from 雪 (xuě) 'snow' and 人 'person', both inherited from Middle Chinese, sjwet and nyin (Guangyun, in Baxter's transcription), which glosses the first 'frozen rain'."
            }
          ]
        },
